+// TestGitIndexDeltaWithExplicitMetaStillHonorsConfigResolvedNames covers
+// the same false-collision risk as
+// TestGitIndexDeltaRequestedWithDistinctConfigNamesBothIndexed, but with
+// an explicit -meta name supplied too: a repository's own git config
+// (zoekt.name) overrides even an explicit -meta name, so two repositories
+// invoked with the same -meta name can still resolve to two distinct,
+// non-colliding effective names, and -delta must not reject either of
